# Felix-attack.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Felixopedes (Empath, polearm). Replaces the
# zombies_landing profile's
#
#   incant 118 (m5), trip target (s7), attack target(xx)
#
# with a single hunting command:
#
#   script Felix-attack
#
# bigshot pauses itself, runs this once against the target it already has
# locked, then resumes to loot / wander / retarget -- so this does ONE pass and
# returns; bigshot re-invokes it every pass while the target is still up. Death
# is read off GameObj status (what bigshot itself uses), not a per-creature
# kill-message regex.
#
# Each pass, same order as the profile line:
#
#   1. Web (118), once per target: recast until it lands (endroll over 100) or
#      WEB_MAX_TRIES misses, skipped if the target is already webbed. Checked
#      against Felix's own logs: all 178 casts that rolled 101+ said "becomes
#      ensnared", all 31 that rolled 100 or less said "The wisps dissipate
#      harmlessly". Targeted Web costs 5 mana (the profile's m5), and every cast
#      is gated on the live checkmana right before it goes out -- casting
#      without the full cost in hand overexerts. Short on mana just skips Web;
#      melee doesn't need it.
#   2. Trip, unless the target is already lying down, or Trip isn't available
#      (CMan.available? -- known, enough stamina, not overexerted; bigshot gates
#      its own trip the same way). A webbed target takes a big bonus against it
#      (+114 on 10/27, knocked the zombie flat). Waits out the Web's cast
#      roundtime first: on 10/27 bigshot sent trip one second early, got "Wait
#      1 seconds." and skipped it.
#   3. Attack. Every pass ends here, so every pass sends a real
#      roundtime-incurring command -- that roundtime is what paces bigshot's
#      next call (an instant silent exit makes bigshot re-run the script in a
#      tight loop -- see Brayis-attack.lic's 2026-09-11 spam note).
#
# Down / webbed are read off the live creature status (Creature[id], the same
# <crtrStatus> feed bigshot's npc_prone? uses), not off trip's own messages:
# trip's result varies by roll (a stun, "It is knocked to the ground!", "...and
# falls!", a sprained ankle), so there's no one success line to match.
#
# Both hands empty = disarmed: don't fight bare-handed (Brayis died doing that
# on 10/22) -- ask bigshot to rest instead. Felix-prep.lic stops bigshot if the
# lance can't be readied in town.

# --- knobs -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Methods, not guarded constants, so an edit takes effect on the next pass
# instead of waiting for a Lich restart.

# Targeted Web is a flat 5 (effect-list.xml's 10 is the untargeted room cast).
def web_mana;      5;   end

# Web is an SMR attack; it lands when the endroll (the "== +N") clears 100.
def web_endroll;   101; end
def web_max_tries; 3;   end

# --- patterns ----------------------------------------------------------------

# A wound blocking spellcasting outright -- no roundtime, so retrying is useless.
def cant_cast_wounded
  /can't think clearly enough to prepare a spell/i
end

# First line of every trip reply seen in Felix's logs, so the read stops as
# soon as the game answers.
def trip_reply
  Regexp.union(
    /With a fluid whirl/,                  # the attempt itself
    /is lying down.*awkward proposition/i, # already down: free, no roundtime
    /You cannot trip/i,                    # "You cannot trip a tree viper."
    /fails miserably/i,                    # fumble: hit yourself in the foot
    /bare hands/i,                         # nothing to trip with
    /You can't reach|Trip what\?/i,
    /^\.\.\.wait|^Wait \d+ sec/i           # still in roundtime
  )
end

# Downcased names of creature types that answered "You cannot trip ...", so
# later passes (and later creatures of the same name) skip straight to the
# attack. A global because bigshot re-invokes this script every pass; lasts
# until Lich restarts, or: ;e $felix_no_trip.clear
$felix_no_trip ||= {}

# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Monster-agnostic death check: bigshot itself reads GameObj status, which Lich
# core keeps current from the room/combat XML. A dead creature reads "dead"
# while the corpse lingers, then "gone" once it decays or is looted.
def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

# Live creature statuses, same as bigshot's npc_has_status?: a creature holding
# several statuses at once only advertises ONE of them through GameObj#status
# (webbed + prone may print just "prone"), so prefer Creature[id]. Falls back
# to the status string only when there's no CreatureInstance for this id yet.
def creature_status?(foe, statuses, fallback)
  creature = (defined?(Creature) ? Creature[foe.id] : nil) rescue nil
  return statuses.any? { |s| creature.has_status?(s) } if creature
  !!(foe.status.to_s =~ fallback)
end

# NOT named webbed? / prone? / stunned?: Lich evals a script's methods into
# Lich::Common, and Object's own globals (lib/global_defs.rb's zero-arg
# webbed? etc. -- YOUR status, not the creature's) take priority over them.
# A webbed?(foe) here was silently shadowed and crashed every pass on 10/27.
def foe_webbed?(foe)
  creature_status?(foe, %w[webbed], /webbed/)
end

# Actually off its feet -- trip on one of these is refused ("...is lying down
# -- attempting to trip her would be a rather awkward proposition."). Stunned
# or webbed creatures are still standing, so they still get tripped.
def foe_down?(foe)
  creature_status?(foe, %w[prone sitting kneeling], /prone|lying|sitting|kneeling/)
end

def hands_empty?
  checkright.nil? && checkleft.nil?
end

# Sends cast_cmd and collects every line through the cast roundtime (a single
# dothistimeout only sees the first matching line, not the whole result).
def cast_and_collect(cast_cmd)
  text_lines = []
  put cast_cmd
  end_time = Time.now.to_f + 6
  loop do
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.1
    else
      text_lines << line
      break if line =~ /Cast Roundtime \d+ Sec|Roundtime: \d+ sec/i || line =~ cant_cast_wounded
    end
    break if Time.now.to_f >= end_time
  end
  text_lines.join(' ')
end

# Web (118) at foe until it lands or web_max_tries casts miss. Once it lands,
# misses out, or a wound blocks casting, $felix_web_done holds this target's id
# so later passes don't recast. Short on mana leaves it unset: the next pass
# tries again if mana has come back. A miss and an armor-hindrance failure
# ("Your armor prevents the spell from working correctly.") both just count as
# a try. The foe_webbed? check at the top of each try also catches a landing whose
# "ensnared" line arrived after the cast roundtime line.
def land_web(foe)
  return if $felix_web_done == foe.id.to_i

  tries = 0
  while tries < web_max_tries
    break if target_dead?(foe) || foe_webbed?(foe)
    return if checkmana < web_mana
    fput "release" if checkprep != "None"
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    return if checkmana < web_mana   # last gate right before the cast
    text = cast_and_collect("incant 118")
    if text =~ cant_cast_wounded
      echo "a wound is blocking spellcasting -- skipping Web, fighting on"
      break
    end
    tries += 1
    roll = (text =~ /o100 roll:.*?==\s*\+?(-?\d+)/ ? Regexp.last_match(1).to_i : nil)
    break if text =~ /becomes ensnared/i || (roll && roll >= web_endroll)
  end
  $felix_web_done = foe.id.to_i
  waitcastrt?
end

def trip_immune?(foe)
  $felix_no_trip.key?(foe.name.to_s.downcase)
end

def mark_trip_immune(foe)
  name = foe.name.to_s.downcase
  return if $felix_no_trip.key?(name)
  $felix_no_trip[name] = true
  echo "#{name} can't be tripped -- skipping trip on it from now on"
end

# One trip attempt at foe. Doesn't look at whether it knocked the target down
# -- the next pass reads that off foe_down? -- so a miss just means the next
# pass trips again while the target is still standing.
def try_trip(foe)
  return if target_dead?(foe) || foe_down?(foe) || trip_immune?(foe)
  return unless CMan.available?("trip")

  waitrt?
  waitcastrt?
  result = dothistimeout("cman trip ##{foe.id}", 3, trip_reply).to_s
  if result =~ /^\.\.\.wait|^Wait \d+ sec/i
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    result = dothistimeout("cman trip ##{foe.id}", 3, trip_reply).to_s
  end
  mark_trip_immune(foe) if result =~ /You cannot trip/i
  waitrt?
end

def finish_attack(foe)
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  waitrt?
  waitcastrt?
  fput "attack ##{foe.id}"
  waitrt?
end

# --- main --------------------------------------------------------------------

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && t.name !~ /animated/ }

# nothing (live) to hit -- hand control straight back to bigshot, which loots
exit if target_dead?(foe)

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i

waitrt?
waitcastrt?

exit if target_dead?(foe)

if hands_empty?
  echo "########## DISARMED -- nothing in either hand ##########"
  echo "## not fighting bare-handed -- asking bigshot to rest"
  $bigshot_should_rest = true
  $rest_reason = "Disarmed"
  exit
end

# The profile hunts in offensive (bigshot normally sets it before calling this;
# no-op then). Web is SMR and doesn't care; trip and the attack do.
fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"

# If Web or trip ever raises, still attack. On 10/27 a crash on the first line
# of land_web (webbed? -- see the helpers note) made every pass exit instantly:
# bigshot re-ran it several times a second and Felix never swung while a zombie
# clawed at him. Report the error, but keep fighting.
begin
  land_web(foe)
  try_trip(foe)
rescue StandardError => e
  echo "Felix-attack: #{e.class}: #{e.message} (#{Array(e.backtrace).first}) -- skipping Web/trip this pass"
end
finish_attack(foe)
